{"id":"sc900_p2_q021","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"Azure virtual network segmentation","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"An organization wants two application tiers in Azure to be separated into different network segments so traffic between them can be controlled. Which Azure concept directly provides this logical network segmentation?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Purview labels"},{"id":"a","text":"Virtual networks and subnets"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Entra access reviews"},{"id":"d","text":"Compliance Manager"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Azure virtual networks and subnets provide logical network segmentation so workloads can be separated and traffic between segments can be controlled.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["azure virtual network segmentation","azure_virtual_network_segmentation"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_virtual_network_segmentation","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_virtual_network_segmentation","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q022","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"network security groups","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A team needs allow/deny rules for traffic entering and leaving a specific Azure subnet or network interface. Which control is designed for that scope?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"Service Trust Portal"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Defender for Identity"},{"id":"a","text":"Network Security Group"},{"id":"d","text":"Retention policy"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Network Security Groups contain security rules that allow or deny network traffic and can be associated with Azure subnets or network interfaces.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["network security groups","network_security_groups"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"network_security_groups","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"network_security_groups","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q023","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"Azure Firewall","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which requirement points to Azure Firewall rather than a network security group?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"Periodic review of group membership"},{"id":"c","text":"Classification of sensitive documents"},{"id":"d","text":"Time-limited activation of directory roles"},{"id":"a","text":"Centralized managed network filtering with stateful firewall capabilities across Azure network traffic"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Azure Firewall is a managed, stateful firewall service used for centralized network traffic filtering. Network Security Groups provide distributed allow/deny rules at subnet or interface scope.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["azure firewall","azure_firewall"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_firewall","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_firewall","stem_style":"distinction_comparison","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q024","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"Azure Web Application Firewall","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A public web application needs protection specifically against common HTTP-based attacks such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting. Which Azure control best fits?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Azure Web Application Firewall"},{"id":"b","text":"Azure Bastion"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Entra ID Protection"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Purview Audit"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Azure Web Application Firewall protects web applications at the application layer against common web exploits such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["azure web application firewall","azure_web_application_firewall"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_web_application_firewall","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_web_application_firewall","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q025","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"Azure Bastion","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Why can Azure Bastion reduce the exposure of administrative access to Azure virtual machines?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"It replaces all identity authentication"},{"id":"c","text":"It classifies sensitive files"},{"id":"d","text":"It provides DLP for email"},{"id":"a","text":"It provides managed RDP/SSH connectivity without requiring each target VM to expose a public IP for that access"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Azure Bastion provides managed RDP and SSH access to virtual machines through the Azure platform, reducing the need to expose target VMs directly through public IP addresses.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["azure bastion","azure_bastion"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_bastion","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_bastion","stem_style":"direct_concept","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q026","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"Azure Key Vault","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A web service needs to retrieve a TLS certificate and an application secret from a centrally managed Azure service instead of storing them in source code. Which service should it use?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Sentinel"},{"id":"c","text":"Access Reviews"},{"id":"a","text":"Azure Key Vault"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Purview eDiscovery"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Azure Key Vault is designed to safeguard and manage secrets, cryptographic keys, and certificates for applications and services.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["azure key vault","azure_key_vault"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_key_vault","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_key_vault","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q027","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_security_management","subobjective":"Microsoft Defender for Cloud","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which Microsoft service provides cloud security posture management together with workload protection capabilities for cloud resources?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Entra ID"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Purview"},{"id":"d","text":"Service Trust Portal"},{"id":"a","text":"Microsoft Defender for Cloud"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Microsoft Defender for Cloud combines cloud security posture management with cloud workload protection capabilities.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"tags":["microsoft defender for cloud","microsoft_defender_for_cloud"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"microsoft_defender_for_cloud","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_security_management","semantic_family_id":"microsoft_defender_for_cloud","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q028","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_security_management","subobjective":"cloud security posture management","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A security team is reviewing secure-score-style posture findings and configuration recommendations before an attack occurs. Which security discipline is this activity primarily part of?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Cloud security posture management"},{"id":"b","text":"eDiscovery"},{"id":"c","text":"Federation"},{"id":"d","text":"Multifactor authentication"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Cloud security posture management continuously evaluates cloud configurations and posture, surfacing recommendations and posture measurements that help reduce exposure.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"tags":["cloud security posture management","cloud_security_posture_management"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"cloud_security_posture_management","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_security_management","semantic_family_id":"cloud_security_posture_management","stem_style":"distinction_comparison","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q029","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_security_management","subobjective":"security policies standards and recommendations","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"What is the purpose of security standards and recommendations in a cloud security posture workflow?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Evaluate resources against desired security controls and identify actions that can improve posture"},{"id":"b","text":"Issue authentication tokens to users"},{"id":"c","text":"Store TLS private keys"},{"id":"d","text":"Preserve documents for a legal case"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Security standards and recommendations help assess resource configurations against desired controls and direct remediation that improves security posture.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"tags":["security policies standards recommendations","security_policies_standards_recommendations"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"security_policies_standards_recommendations","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_security_management","semantic_family_id":"security_policies_standards_recommendations","stem_style":"direct_concept","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p2_q030","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_security_management","subobjective":"cloud workload protection","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which scenario is most closely associated with cloud workload protection rather than posture management alone?","choices":[{"id":"b","text":"Calculating how many compliance improvement actions are complete"},{"id":"c","text":"Recertifying guest group membership"},{"id":"a","text":"Detecting and responding to threats affecting running cloud workloads"},{"id":"d","text":"Applying a retention label to a document"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Cloud workload protection focuses on protecting running workloads from threats, complementing posture management's emphasis on configuration and exposure reduction.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"tags":["cloud workload protection","cloud_workload_protection"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase2-batch-03","blueprint_leaf_id":"cloud_workload_protection","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_security_management","semantic_family_id":"cloud_workload_protection","stem_style":"distinction_comparison","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
